  "termGrain": "Grain",
  "termGrainText": "The direction of the wood fibres, that of the lines you see along the board.",
  "termGrainUse": "Know which way to plane, sand or cut: with the grain, the wood comes out smooth; against it, it tears.",
  "termEdge": "Edge",
  "termEdgeText": "The narrow face of a board or panel, across its thickness.",
  "termEdgeUse": "Talk about the piece clearly: you screw into the edge, glue on edge banding, true an edge with a plane.",
  "termChamfer": "Chamfer",
  "termChamferText": "Small bevel cut on an arris, most often at 45°.",
  "termChamferUse": "Take off a sharp arris: fewer splinters and chips, and paint or varnish holds better on the corner.",
  "termKerf": "Kerf",
  "termKerfText": "The slot the blade leaves as it cuts, as wide as its teeth.",
  "termKerfUse": "Know which side of the line to saw: those few millimetres turn to sawdust, they must fall in the offcut.",
  "termPilotHole": "Pilot hole",
  "termPilotHoleText": "Thin hole drilled before screwing, smaller than the screw's core.",
  "termPilotHoleUse": "Guide the screw and stop the wood splitting, especially near an end or in hardwood.",
  "termCountersink": "Countersink",
  "termCountersinkText": "Cone-shaped widening at the mouth of a hole, the shape of a screw head.",
  "termCountersinkUse": "So the screw head sits flush or slightly below, instead of sticking out.",
  "termFurring": "Furring channel",
  "termFurringText": "Flattened U-shaped metal profile, screwed or hung under a ceiling or against a wall.",
  "termFurringUse": "Carry plasterboard nice and flat, even when the ceiling or wall behind isn't.",
  "termVapourBarrier": "Vapour barrier",
  "termVapourBarrierText": "Film or membrane laid on the warm side of the insulation, joints taped.",
  "termVapourBarrierUse": "Stop the room's vapour getting into the insulation, where it would condense and soak it.",
  "gesturesTitle": "Basic techniques",
  "gesturesHelp": "Saw, plane, drill, screw, sand, cut a mortise, run a sealant bead: the animated technique, the steps and the mistake to avoid.",
  "gesturesIntro": "Each technique plays as an animated sketch. Watch it, read the three steps, then try it first on an offcut.",
