  "gestureSaw": "Saw straight",
  "gestureSawUse": "Cut a board or batten to the right length, straight and clean.",
  "gestureSaw1": "Mark the line with pencil and square, on the top and on the edge.",
  "gestureSaw2": "Put the blade against the line, on the waste side, and start with two or three pull strokes towards you, blade at 45°.",
  "gestureSaw3": "Saw with the whole length of the blade, without pressing. Slow down at the end and hold the offcut so it doesn't tear the wood.",
  "gestureSawMistake": "Sawing on the line: the piece ends up short by the thickness of the blade.",
  "gestureSawLine": "waste side of the line",
  "gestureSawAngle": "blade at 45°",
  "gesturePlane": "Plane",
  "gesturePlaneUse": "Take off a thin layer to fit a piece: a door that rubs, an edge to straighten.",
  "gesturePlane1": "Set the iron so it barely sticks out: the shaving should be as thin as paper.",
  "gesturePlane2": "Press on the front of the plane at the start of the stroke, on the back at the end.",
  "gesturePlane3": "Plane with the grain, in one movement, from one end of the piece to the other.",
  "gesturePlaneMistake": "Planing against the grain: the wood tears instead of smoothing. If it catches, turn the piece round.",
  "gesturePlaneGrain": "with the grain",
  "gesturePlaneShaving": "even stroke",
  "gestureDrill": "Drill",
  "gestureDrillUse": "Make a clean hole for a screw, a wall plug or a cable.",
  "gestureDrill1": "Mark the centre with a punch: the bit won't wander when starting.",
  "gestureDrill2": "Hold the drill straight, start slowly, then speed up.",
  "gestureDrill3": "For a clean exit, clamp a scrap of wood under the piece.",
  "gestureDrillMistake": "Forcing the drill: the bit overheats and breaks. Let it advance and pull it out to clear the chips.",
  "gestureDrillStraight": "nice and straight",
  "gestureDrillBacking": "scrap underneath",
  "gestureScrew": "Screw",
  "gestureScrewUse": "Join two pieces of wood without splitting them.",
  "gestureScrew1": "Drill a pilot hole a little thinner than the screw, especially near an end or in hardwood.",
  "gestureScrew2": "Countersink the hole so the head sits flush.",
  "gestureScrew3": "Drive with the bit pushed well into the head and a low torque setting; finish by hand if needed.",
  "gestureScrewMistake": "Screwing without a pilot hole near an end: the wood splits.",
  "gestureScrewHead": "head in the countersink",
  "gestureScrewPieces": "two pieces pulled tight",
  "gestureSand": "Sand",
  "gestureSandUse": "Make a surface smooth before a finish, or remove a mark.",
  "gestureSand1": "Start at 80 grit if the wood is marked, then 120, then 180: don't skip more than one grit at a time.",
  "gestureSand2": "Sand with the grain, in overlapping passes, without pressing: the sander's weight is enough.",
  "gestureSand3": "Dust off between grits: a grain left on the wood scratches on the next pass.",
  "gestureSandMistake": "Staying in the same place: the sander digs a dip that will show under the varnish.",
  "gestureSandWeight": "without pressing",
  "gestureSandGrain": "80, 120 then 180",
  "gestureChisel": "Cut a mortise",
