  "gestureCutBoardUse": "Cut a plasterboard to the right width without a saw, with a knife.",
  "gestureCutBoard1": "Mark the line on the paper face, with a straightedge or level held against it.",
  "gestureCutBoard2": "Cut the paper with the knife along the straightedge, in one or two passes, without trying to go through.",
  "gestureCutBoard3": "Snap the board sharply along the cut, then slice the paper on the back and run a rasp along the edge.",
  "gestureCutBoardMistake": "Cutting freehand without a straightedge: the edge wobbles and the joint shows on the ceiling.",
  "gestureCutBoardRule": "straightedge against the line",
  "gestureCutBoardSnap": "then snap it",
  "gestureMitre": "Cut a 45° mitre",
  "gestureMitreUse": "Make two skirting boards or two mouldings meet in a corner, with no gap.",
  "gestureMitre1": "Mark the length on the edge that touches the wall, and the cut direction with a slanted line.",
  "gestureMitre2": "Hold the piece against the back of the box, visible face towards you, and hold it firmly.",
  "gestureMitre3": "Slide the saw into the 45° slot, start with a pull stroke, then saw without forcing down to the bottom.",
  "gestureMitreMistake": "Cutting both pieces the same way: the corner opens up. Always offer up both pieces before the second cut.",
  "gestureMitreSlot": "45° slot",
  "gestureMitreBack": "piece held at the back",
  "gestureLaser": "Mark with a laser level",
  "gestureLaserUse": "Mark a level line all round a room, for an edge angle, a splashback or aligned shelves.",
  "gestureLaser1": "Put the laser on a tripod or stable support, at roughly the right height, and let it level itself.",
  "gestureLaser2": "Measure the height in one place, set the laser to it, then mark the line in pencil every 50 cm.",
  "gestureLaser3": "Join the marks with a straightedge: the line follows the level, even if the floor or ceiling isn't straight.",
  "gestureLaserMistake": "Looking into the beam or pointing it at someone: a site laser damages the eye.",
