  "defectSplitHelp": "Crack at the end of a board, going through the thickness. It often continues under the surface: cut off the split and 5 cm more.",
  "defectCheckHelp": "Small surface cracks, from drying too fast. Harmless if they stay on the surface; planing often makes them disappear.",
  "defectTwistHelp": "The two ends aren't in the same plane: laid flat, the board rocks on a corner. It's the defect that's hardest to correct.",
  "defectBowHelp": "The board curves along its length. Sight along it from one end or lay a 2 m straightedge on it and measure the biggest gap.",
  "defectCupHelp": "The face hollows across its width, like a roof tile. Common on wide boards; a narrow board or one ripped in two behaves better.",
  "defectMoistureHelp": "Timber that's too damp shrinks and warps as it dries in your home. A pin moisture meter gives the reading in seconds; otherwise leave the wood in the room for one to two weeks before working it.",
