  "tradeInsulation1": "Squashing the wool to make it fit: it insulates less.",
  "tradeInsulation2": "A torn or badly taped vapour barrier: condensation soaks the insulation.",
  "tradeInsulation3": "Leaving gaps between the batts: as many thermal bridges.",
  "tradeDrywall1": "Spacing the studs more than 60 cm apart: the partition sounds hollow and moves.",
  "tradeDrywall2": "Screwing too deep: the head goes through the paper and no longer holds.",
  "tradeDrywall3": "Overloading the taped joints with filler: endless sanding and thick spots.",
  "tradeTiling1": "Laying on a surface that isn't flat: the tiles are no longer flush.",
  "tradeTiling2": "Spreading too much adhesive at once: it skins over before the tile is laid.",
  "tradeTiling3": "Starting from a wall that isn't straight instead of a line marked down the middle.",
  "tradeJoinery1": "A door set that isn't plumb: the door opens or closes on its own.",
  "tradeJoinery2": "Too much expanding foam: as it swells, it distorts the frame.",
  "tradeJoinery3": "Forgetting the gap under the door, for air and for the future floor.",
  "tradePlumbing1": "Overtightening a fitting: the washer gets cut or the nut cracks.",
  "tradePlumbing2": "Taking things apart without turning off the water and draining the pipe.",
  "tradePlumbing3": "A waste pipe without enough slope: it blocks.",
  "tradeElectricity1": "Assuming the power is off without checking it with a tester, on every wire.",
  "tradeElectricity2": "Changing a wire's size or a breaker's rating.",
  "tradeElectricity3": "A loose terminal: it heats up, with a risk of fire.",
  "tradeProPartPlumbing": "On your own: change a trap, a flexible hose, a washer, water off. Leave it to a pro: concealed supplies, waste pipes in walls, and anything to do with gas.",
  "tradeProPartElectricity": "On your own, power off and checked: replace like for like. Leave it to a pro: consumer unit, new circuit, bathroom. Whether a new or rewired installation needs an inspection (Consuel in France) depends on your case.",
